{:edb/db-before-t 1942 :edb/db-after-t 1943 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535255 50 #inst "2026-10-08T20:31:30.511Z" 13194139535255 true] [17592186128784 1100 "Express the triple integral\n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_{R} (x+y+z)^2 \\: \\textrm{d}V$\nover the box\n$R = \\bigg\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\: -1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: 0\\leq z \\leq 2 \\bigg\\}$\nas a repeated integral of the form\n$\\displaystyle \\int_a^b \\int_c^d \\int_e^f \\ldots \\: \\textrm{d}y\\: \\textrm{d}z\\: \\textrm{d}x$." 13194139535255 false] [17592186128784 1100 "Express the triple integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \n\\iiint\\limits_{R} (x+y+z)^2 \\: \\textrm{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box\n\n$$\nR = \\bigg\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\: -1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: 0\\leq z \\leq 2 \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nas a repeated integral of the form \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \n\\int_a^b  \\int_c^d  \\int_e^f \\ldots \\: \\textrm{d}y\\:  \\textrm{d}z\\:  \\textrm{d}x .\n$$" 13194139535255 true] [17592186128784 1145 "Given the limits for $x,y$, and $z$, we can express our triple integral as a repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∭_(R)(x + y + z)^{2}dV &= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}(x + y + z)^{2}dydzdx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535255 false] [17592186128784 1145 "Given the limits for $x,y,$ and $z,$ we can express our triple integral as a repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(x+y+z)^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(x+y+z)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535255 true] [17592186128789 1100 "By integrating first with respect to $z$, then $x$, and then $y$, evaluate the triple integral\n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R z-xy \\: \\mathrm{d}V$\nover the rectangular box $R = \\left\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\:0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: -1 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\: 1 \\leq z \\leq 3 \\right\\}$." 13194139535255 false] [17592186128789 1100 "By integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R z-xy  \\: \\mathrm{d}V\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R = \\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\:0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: -1 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\: 1 \\leq z \\leq 3 \\right\\}.$" 13194139535255 true] [17592186128789 1145 "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} z-xy \\: \\textrm{d}V\n= \n\\int_{-1}^{1} \\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{1}^{3} z-xy \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y,$ we write $\\textrm d V = \\textrm d z\\:\\textrm d x\\:\\textrm d y.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}z-xy\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}z-xy\\,dz]dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{2}-xyz]}_{z=1}^{z=3}\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(9-1)-xy(3-1)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-2xy\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-2xy\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-2yx\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[4x-y{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}4(2-0)-y({2}^{2}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}8-4y\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}8-4y\\,dy & =[8y-2{y}^{2}]_{y=-1}^{y=1} \\\\  & =8(1-(-1))-2({1}^{2}-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot 2-2(1-1) \\\\  & =16-0 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535255 true] [17592186128789 1145 "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} z-xy \\: \\textrm{d}V = \\int_{-1}^{1} \\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{1}^{3} z-xy \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $z$, then $x$, and then $y$, we write\n\n$$\n\\textrm d V = \\textrm d z\\:\\textrm d x\\:\\textrm d y\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}∫_{1}^{3}z - xydzdxdy &= ∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}[∫_{1}^{3}z - xydz]dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}[\\frac{1}{2}z^{2} - xyz]_{z = 1}^{z = 3}dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(9 - 1) - xy(3 - 1)dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}4 - 2xydxdy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}4 - 2xydxdy &= ∫_{-1}^{1}[∫_{0}^{2}4 - 2yxdx]dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}[4x - yx^{2}]_{x = 0}^{x = 2}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}4(2 - 0) - y(2^{2} - 0)dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}8 - 4ydy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{-1}^{1}8 - 4ydy &= [8y - 2y^{2}]_{y =-1}^{y = 1} \\\\\n&= 8(1 - (-1)) - 2(1^{2} - (-1)^{2}) \\\\\n&= 8 \\cdot 2 - 2(1 - 1) \\\\\n&= 16 - 0 \\\\\n&= 16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535255 false] [17592186128949 1100 "Evaluate the triple integral\n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_{R} y \\cos{x} \\sin{z} \\: \\textrm{d}V$\nover the box $R = \\bigg\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq \\pi \\bigg\\}$." 13194139535255 false] [17592186128949 1100 "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \n\\iiint\\limits_{R} y \\cos{x} \\sin{z} \\: \\textrm{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box $R = \\bigg\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq \\pi \\bigg\\}.$" 13194139535255 true] [17592186128949 1145 "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∭_(R)y\\cos x\\sin zdV &= ∫_{0}^{π}∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{π/2}y\\cos x\\sin zdxdydz\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration\n\n$$\nR = \\left[0,\\pi/2\\right]\\times[0,1]\\times\\left[0,\\pi\\right]\n$$\n\nis a rectangular box, and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z)$, we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n∫_{0}^{π/2}\\cos xdx∫_{0}^{1}ydy∫_{0}^{π}\\sin zdz\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{π/2}\\cos xdx∫_{0}^{1}ydy∫_{0}^{π}\\sin zdz &= [\\sin x]_{0}^{π/2} \\cdot [\\frac{y^{2}}{2}]_{0}^{1} \\cdot [- \\cos z]_{0}^{π} \\\\\n&= (1 - 0) \\cdot (\\frac{1}{2} - 0) \\cdot (1 - (-1)) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535255 false] [17592186128949 1145 "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R = \\left[0,\\pi/2\\right]\\times[0,1]\\times\\left[0,\\pi\\right]$ is a rectangular box, and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z & =[\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z]_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-0)\\cdot (1-(-1)) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535255 true] [17592186129131 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340047 13194139535255 true] [17592186129131 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340054 13194139535255 true] [17592186129131 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340082 13194139535255 true] [17592186129131 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340089 13194139535255 true] [17592186129207 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340061 13194139535255 true] [17592186129207 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340068 13194139535255 true] [17592186129207 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340075 13194139535255 true] [17592186129207 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340124 13194139535255 true] [17592186129207 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340131 13194139535255 true] [17592186129211 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340096 13194139535255 true] [17592186129211 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340103 13194139535255 true] [17592186129211 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340110 13194139535255 true] [17592186129211 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340117 13194139535255 true] [17592186129450 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535255 true] [17592186129450 1100 "By integrating first with respect to $z$, then $x$, and then $y$, evaluate the triple integral\n\n$∭_(R)(x - y)e^{z}dV$\nover the rectangular box $R = {(x, y, z): 0 \\le x \\le 1,-1 \\le y \\le 0, \\ln 2 \\le z \\le 2}$." 13194139535255 false] [17592186129450 1100 "By integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\le z\\le 2}.$" 13194139535255 true] [17592186129450 1145 "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{2}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{2}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{2}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dz]dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[(x-y){e}^{z}]_{z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{z=2}\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)({e}^{2}-2)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)({e}^{2}-2)\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)({e}^{2}-2)\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[({e}^{2}-2){\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2){[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-xy]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2)[\\frac{1}{2}(1-0)-(1-0)y]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2)(\\frac{1}{2}-y)dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2)(\\frac{1}{2}-y)dy & =({e}^{2}-2){\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{1}{2}-y\\,dy \\\\  & =({e}^{2}-2){[\\frac{1}{2}y-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=-1}^{y=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-2}{2}(0-(-1)+1) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535255 true] [17592186129675 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535255 true] [17592186129675 1100 "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$∭_(R)\\frac{e^{z + y}}{x}dV$,\nover the box $R = {(x, y, z): 1 \\le x \\le e, 0 \\le y \\le \\ln 3, 0 \\le z \\le \\ln 2}$." 13194139535255 false] [17592186129675 1100 "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}V,\\,\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,0\\le z\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" 13194139535255 true] [17592186129675 1145 "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[1,e]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{e}^{z}\\cdot {e}^{y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z & ={[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]}_{1}^{e}\\cdot {[{e}^{y}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot {[{e}^{z}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (3-1)\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535255 true] [17592186340047 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340048 13194139535255 true] [17592186340047 1089 "q-161274" 13194139535255 true] [17592186340047 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535255 true] [17592186340047 1100 "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{y{e}^{z}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\le x\\le \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡5}.$" 13194139535255 true] [17592186340047 1113 #uuid "ffd92837-16f0-58e8-90f2-50cab6f18326" 13194139535255 true] [17592186340047 1145 "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{y{e}^{z}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{y{e}^{z}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}]\\times [0,1]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡5]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{y{e}^{z}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot y\\cdot {e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z & ={[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot [{e}^{z}]_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5} \\\\  & =(-\\sqrt{2}+2\\sqrt{2})\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-0)\\cdot (5-1) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535255 true] [17592186340048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340049 13194139535255 true] [17592186340048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340050 13194139535255 true] [17592186340048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340051 13194139535255 true] [17592186340048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340052 13194139535255 true] [17592186340048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340053 13194139535255 true] [17592186340048 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535255 true] [17592186340048 1041 "selection" 13194139535255 true] [17592186340048 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340051 13194139535255 true] [17592186340048 1110 #uuid "4a54a42a-c42a-5da8-b8b4-f017587eb533" 13194139535255 true] [17592186340049